{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789836658,"nonce":"ohJG9vCb0EerAS/5iZSLsw7zlCM=","title":"Five zynml test files do not compile under edition 2024","message":"`std::env::set_var` and `remove_var` are unsafe in edition 2024 and\nthese call them bare, so `cargo test -p zynml` fails to build and the\nwhole crate's tests stop running: autovec, hot_reload_rollback,\nparallel_dispatch_end_to_end, vector_lane_width,\nvectorize_expression_trees.\n\nEach needs the calls wrapped, or the switch passed to the child process\ninstead of set on the test's own environment (the tests run in parallel,\nso a process-wide variable is a race anyway).","files":null}]}